        "category": "offensive",
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>(attack, manipulate, range 200 feet) @Damage[6d12[piercing]], single target, @Check[reflex|dc:22]. On a failed save, the harpoon becomes lodged in the target’s body. The target can remove the harpoon with a DC 22 check to Escape or Force Open, but on a failure, the target takes @Damage[6d4[piercing]] damage. As long as the harpoon cannon bolt remains lodged, the target cannot move more than 200 feet away from the harpoon cannon. If the harpoon cannon bolt is embedded in a creature that isn’t swimming, one member of the crew can attempt to Trip the creature by tugging on the rope if all other crew members Aid. On a failure, the bolt rips free, causing @Damage[4d4[piercing]] damage to the target but releasing it.</p>"
